60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Based on our findings, Option B risks social friction and Option C is an administrative nightmare that kills attendance. Option A is the only logical choice to ensure stability and inclusivity. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The evidence is overwhelming. Option C is a recipe for treasurer burnout, and Option B creates social divisions. Option A is the most rational and efficient path forward. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"While the imbalance in attendance remains a concern, the risks associated with the other options are too great. For the sake of the club's stability and the treasurer's well-being, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,I've seen how per-event charges kill the mood and make people hesitate. We need to remove that barrier and make belonging automatic again. Option A is the only way to do that. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"It's the only way to make sure we actually have the money for those fixed costs without guessing. No more headaches, no more mess. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Since we have reached a unanimous consensus on Option A, there is no further need for debate. The logic is sound and the evidence supports this decision.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
